--
Was KNOWNBUG (crash, then nondet values).  Full fix history: (1) crash:
per-base recovery + graceful make_ptr_typecast; (2) nondet has_value():
base NSDMIs applied in synthesized derived constructors
(cpp11_base_nsdmi_implicit_ctor); (3) dropped _Optional_base: the
destructibility probe `decltype(declval<T&>().~T())` now resolves in
nested instantiation contexts -- trivial implicit destructors use the
no-op dummy ([class.dtor]/1,6), the ~_Tp substitution prefers the
current class scope's binding ([expr.prim.id.dtor]/2), and the
destructor name extraction is angle-aware (was spelling `~allocator`
for basic_string, see cpp17_dtor_sfinae_base_spec).
